Third-party notices — myne-server
=================================

The shipped artefact is the OCI image built by `Dockerfile`, whose digest is the
verification unit (SYNC-28). Three answers about what it redistributes, and two
of them are not the obvious ones.


1. The Go module graph is empty
-------------------------------

`go.mod` declares a module and a toolchain and nothing else, and the repository
has no `go.sum`: the server is pure standard library today. No third-party Go
module is redistributed by this binary.

Verify:

  go list -m all        # the module itself, then nothing
  ls go.sum             # absent by design, not by accident


2. Two binaries this repository pins and copies in
--------------------------------------------------

The image bundles a backup engine and its transport. Both are fetched at build
time by `scripts/fetchtool`, each pinned by sha256 in the Dockerfile (the SYNC-20
pin-by-digest discipline), and both are REDISTRIBUTED inside the shipped image.
They have no row in the Go module graph, so nothing else in this repository
would have mentioned them.

